Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m900: Lock LPC, CLKRUN and PLTRST pads in ramstage

The pad list (GPP_A1-A6, GPP_A8, GPP_A9, GPP_B13) comes from the M900
TEST= description in merged Gerrit 90885, patch set 8. The original
pull, reset, and native-function settings are from the pinned 26.09
src/mainboard/lenovo/m900/gpio.h:15-20,22-23,53 -- the locked lines only.
Gerrit 90885 changes only Skylake Kconfig; it does not contain an M900
board-table patch.

Note that the list covers more than the LPC address/data and PLTRST pads:
GPP_A8 and GPP_A9 are also in it. They are the pads the ThinkPad variant
tables name -CLKRUN and LPCCLK_EC_24M, and kukri's skl_kbl.c names the
same two CLKRUN and CLKOUT_LPC0; upstream's 90885 TEST= line groups all
nine as "LPC pins and PLTRST#".

GPP_A7 is deliberately left unlocked, because the 90885 M900 test does
not name it. On the SKL/KBL ThinkPads GPP_A7 is -TPM_IRQ, so the M900
list is a strict subset of what upstream 93324 locks for those boards,
and the pad most like -TPM_IRQ is the one this leaves open.

This is a separate downstream adaptation of that reported test, not
upstream-authored board code. PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK also changes the reset
domain to PWROK
(src/soc/intel/common/block/include/intelblocks/gpio_defs.h:224-229),
which requires board-level validation.

Intel's GPIO Configuration Best Practices, document 834810 (listed in
doc/TPM_GPIO_Reset_Approaches.md, Appendix C), recommends locking
security-sensitive pad configurations before third-party code runs.
It does not identify this board's pads or the Skylake PCH-H offsets;
those come from the upstream M900 test and Gerrit 95661 respectively.

Based-on: https://review.coreboot.org/c/coreboot/+/90885
Origin verified 2026-10-07T00:33:08-04:00: upstream MERGED, local board
adaptation not submitted upstream.
---

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m900/gpio.h b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m900/gpio.h
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m900/gpio.h
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m900/gpio.h
@@ -13,13 +13,13 @@ static const struct pad_config gpio_table[] = {
 	/* ------- GPIO Group GPP_A ------- */
 	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A0, NONE, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A1, UP_20K, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A2, UP_20K, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A3, UP_20K, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A4, UP_20K, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A5, NONE, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A6, NONE, PLTRST, NF1),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A1, UP_20K, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A2, UP_20K, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A3, UP_20K, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A4, UP_20K, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A5, NONE, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A6, NONE, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
 	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A7, NONE, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A8, NONE, PLTRST, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A9, DN_20K, PLTRST, NF1),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A8, NONE, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_A9, DN_20K, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
 	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A10, DN_20K, PLTRST, NF1),
 	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_A11, NONE, PLTRST, NF1),
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ static const struct pad_config gpio_table[] = {
 	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_B10, NONE, PLTRST, NF1),
 	PAD_CFG_GPO(GPP_B11, 0, PLTRST),
 	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_B12, NONE, DEEP, NF1),
-	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_B13, NONE, DEEP, NF1),
+	PAD_CFG_NF_LOCK(GPP_B13, NONE, NF1, LOCK_FULL),
 	PAD_CFG_NF(GPP_B14, DN_20K, PLTRST, NF1),
 	PAD_CFG_GPO(GPP_B15, 0, PLTRST),
 	PAD_CFG_GPO(GPP_B16, 0, PLTRST),
